# HTTP contract

Build every body with `lib/response.ts`.

| Helper | When |
| --- | --- |
| `sendData` | one resource, login, dashboard, health |
| `sendList` | pages. `meta` sits beside `data` |
| `sendFailure` | errors. `data` is `null` except health |

`totalPages` is `0` when `total` is `0`, else `ceil(total / limit)`. Delete and logout are `200` with `data: null`.

| Code | HTTP |
| --- | --- |
| `VALIDATION_ERROR` | 400 |
| `INVALID_CREDENTIALS`, `UNAUTHENTICATED` | 401 |
| `FORBIDDEN` | 403 |
| `DOCTOR_NOT_FOUND`, `PATIENT_NOT_FOUND` | 404 |
| `EMAIL_IN_USE` | 409 |
| `RATE_LIMITED` | 429 |
| `INTERNAL` | 500 |

Health does not throw. A failed database ping calls `sendFailure` with `503`, code `INTERNAL`, and `data` of `status`, `database`, and `datetime`. Every other `INTERNAL` response is `500`.

Unknown paths are `404` / `VALIDATION_ERROR` / `Route not found`. Zod failures use `details: [{ path, message }]`. A 24-hex id that fails Zod is `VALIDATION_ERROR`, not a cast and not a 404.

Zod strips unknown fields. `page` defaults to 1. `limit` is 1–50, default 20. Sort fields are a whitelist on the schema. List routes do not filter the page again in memory.

Register every path in `src/docs/openapi.ts` from the same Zod schemas. Swagger is public at `GET /api/docs`.
